Okay, I updated the patch like this:

* When confronted with a worn bag, mind flayers' attacks have a
one-in-two chance of being converted into a theft attack.

* Also, if you're wearing an unprotected helm, there's a one-in-eight
chance that it'll try and steal THAT.

* NOTE: There's something you ought to know about grease and oilskins.
Greased armour protects against an owlbear's crushing and a mimic's
stickiness, but it does NOT protect against theft. (Wizard mode: empty
your inventory, wear a greased uncursed helmet, then see how long it
takes for the standard monkey to run off with it.) Thus, for internal
consistency purposes, greased or oilskin bags do NOT have a reduced
chance of a mind flayer stealing it.

* 'cubi can also (ask to) remove bags.

* Also improved a couple of message cases involving the words "you're
already wearing".

* After reviewing for a bit, I've decided to not give special treatment
to wearing overly heavy bags of holding. By the same token, the weight
limit on wearing bags has been lifted (you can wear it as long as you
can carry it, just like regular armour.)



